{"name":"Reassurance seeking (rate me threads)","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":1585,"casual":{"lead":["Rate-me threads are forum posts where people share photos and ask for ratings or critiques of their face. The payoff people want is an outside opinion on their attractiveness and a list of what to improve.","Users post photos and receive scores and feedback from other members. Clinically, repeatedly asking others to confirm how you look is described as a behaviour in body dysmorphic disorder, alongside mirror checking and comparing. No studies specific to these threads were found; related research links appearance-focused social media use to body dissatisfaction."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People post front and side photos to a forum thread, read the ratings and comments, and use them to pick things to work on, such as grooming, fitness or skin. Some return repeatedly with updated photos to track changes."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Feedback comes from anonymous strangers and can be harsh. In BDD, repeated reassurance seeking tends to bring short-term relief followed by renewed doubt. Related research links appearance-focused social media use to body dissatisfaction."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Is appearance-related social comparison a causal mechanism underlying appearance-related psychopathology among young adult women? An experimental test.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42748514/","source":"Behaviour research and therapy","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Heart-Focused Anxiety: An Evolutionary Concept Analysis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34225289/","source":"ANS. Advances in nursing science","year":2022,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Tourettic OCD: Current understanding and treatment challenges of a unique endophenotype.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35966462/","source":"Frontiers in psychiatry","year":2