0/"},{"title":"rate me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me.1856440/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260214172627/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me.1856440/"},{"title":"rate me and my friend","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-and-my-friend.1853170/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260212022409/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-and-my-friend.1853170/"},{"title":"rate me pls","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-pls.1851474/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260211221058/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-pls.1851474/"},{"title":"rate me m16","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-m16.1844125/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260207144931/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-m16.1844125/"},{"title":"rate me brutally","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-brutally.1843430/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260210175934/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-brutally.1843430/"},{"title":"rate me 21 61","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-21-61.1840994/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260211223910/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-21-61.1840994/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Body dysmorphic disorder - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_dysmorphic_disorder"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Confidence & presence","chain":["Posting photos for ratings","Short-term reassurance","Ongoing dependence on feedback"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Rate-me threads give people outside opinions on facial attractiveness and ideas for what to improve. The same pattern, repeated reassurance seeking, is listed clinically among BDD behaviours, so feedback that helps one person plan can become a loop for another."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Reassurance seeking, in the clinical sense, is frequently asking others for verbal confirmation about one's appearance. Wikipedia lists it among the repetitive behaviors of body dysmorphic disorder (BDD), alongside mirror checking, comparing and camouflaging.[1]","'Rate me' threads are posts on appearance forums in which users share photos and ask others to rate or critique their looks. Published research specifically on rate-me threads was not located; the clinical description of reassurance seeking in BDD is the closest documented context."],"infobox":[["Type","Behavior / forum post format"],["Clinical context","Reassurance seeking in body dysmorphic disorder"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Wikipedia describes reassurance seeking as a common BDD behavior and notes that heavy selfie-taking and social media use are linked to low self-esteem and body dysmorphic tendencies, with users sometimes seeking validation through likes and comments.[1] A 2020 systematic review cited there found appearance-focused social media use linked to body image dissatisfaction.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on rate-me threads. Cognitive-behavioral therapy for BDD, which includes exposure and response prevention aimed at rituals such as reassurance seeking, has been tested in randomized trials; see CBT for BDD."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Body dysmorphic disorder","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_dysmorphic_disorder","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Rate me be brutal","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-be-brutal.2414457/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260927040548/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-be-brutal.2414457/"},{"title":"Rate me -15","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-15.2043166/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260429153353/https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-15.2043166/"},{"title":"rate me (15years 5.91 ft)","url":"h